  "name": "bisect-version-regression",
  "description": "Bisect a Triton compiler performance or correctness regression reported between two Triton versions (for example 3.5 vs 3.8). Use when a kernel is slower, spills more, or compiles much more slowly after a Triton upgrade, and the culprit commit or change must be found. Tries tritonparse's built-in bisect first when its feasibility checklist passes, and falls back to a file-group revert bisect when the endpoints only exist as internal snapshot trees. Requires a GPU for benchmarking.",
